{"step_index":1770,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:06:56Z","thinking":"Mapping between steps and cells has been established; each markdown header corresponds to the intended code cell. This precise correspondence is crucial for executing the remaining steps correctly. The established mapping will ensure the code executes in the intended order, linking each step to its respective code.\n\n\nThe code for Cell 8 defines functions to download and parse a JSONL dataset from a specified URL, including a system prompt and a raw repository URL for accessing the data. The data retrieval is based on a JSONL file hosted on GitHub, which suggests the presence of curated chain-of-thought security samples. The download function utilizes `urllib.request` to handle the HTTP request. I'm verifying that the expected modules are imported and ready for this task.\n\n\nDownloaded and processed security chain-of-thought (CoT) samples, red team offensive security samples, and identity alignment samples. Each dataset was loaded and prepped by extracting instructions, inputs, and outputs from JSONL files, creating a structured format suitable for training. The system prompt was added to each sample to define the context.\n\n\nThe total training dataset size is calculated based on multiplying the counts of each data category by a specific factor: security records by 5, red team records by 2, and identity records by 4. This expansion aims to give the model a wider range of training examples. The dataset is shuffled, formatted into a text-based representation, and prepared for training.  The breakdown shows the expansion factors and how many distinct training items are present for each category.\n\n\nUpdated the markdown title of Cell 7 to `## Step 4: Prepare Cybersecurity Training Dataset`. Cell 8's content has been updated with the dataset preparation code, and Cell 10's content has been updated with the training code. Cell 8 is now executing. The output will be checked to confirm the expected dataset size.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"send_message","args":{"Message":"Excellent work mapping the cells! Now let's execute the update:\n\n1. Update Cell 7 (header) to:\n`## Step 4: Prepare Cybersecurity Training Dataset`\n\n2. Update Cell 8 (dataset code) with the new GitHub-downloading code.\n3. Update Cell 10 (training code) with `max_steps=65`, `learning_rate=8e-5`.\n\nHere is the exact script to evaluate in `mcp_chrome_devtools_evaluate_script`:\n```javascript\n() => {\n  const cells = colab.global.notebook.cells;\n  \n  // 1. Clean up Cell 7 markdown header\n  cells[7].setText(\"## Step 4: Prepare Cybersecurity Training Dataset\");\n  \n  // 2. Set Cell 8 code (downloads 520 samples from GitHub)\n  const step4Code = `import json\nimport random\nimport urllib.request\nfrom datasets import Dataset\n\nSYSTEM_PROMPT = (\n    \"You are Fluxnat Coder 3B, an elite AI cybersecurity and secure coding intelligence model created by Fluxnat. \"\n    \"Your mission is to perform rigorous source code vulnerability auditing, identify CWE and OWASP Top 10 security flaws, \"\n    \"explain attack surfaces and root causes using detailed step-by-step reasoning, and provide production-ready secure remediations.\"\n)\n\nREPO_RAW = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/k4ran909/Fluxnat-coder/main\"\n\ndef download_jsonl(url):\n    print(f\"[*] Downloading {url.split('/')[-1]}...\")\n    response = urllib.request.urlopen(url)\n    data = response.read().decode('utf-8')\n    records = []\n    for line in data.strip().split('\\\\n'):\n        if line.strip():\n            records.append(json.loads(line))\n    return records\n\n# 1. Download curated security CoT samples (24 samples)\nsecurity_raw = download_jsonl(f\"{REPO_RAW}/data/custom_cot/security_cot.jsonl\")\nsecurity_records = []\nfor item in security_raw:\n    if 'messages' in item:\n        if item['messages'] and item['messages'][0]['role'] == 'system':\n            item['messages'][0]['content'] = SYSTEM_PROMPT\n        security_records.append(item)\nprint(f\"[+] Loaded {len(security_records)} security CoT samples\")\n\n# 2. Download red team offensive security samples (170 samples)\nredteam_raw = download_jsonl(f\"{REPO_RAW}/data/custom_cot/redteam_cot.jsonl\")\nredteam_records = []\nfor item in redteam_raw:\n    instruction = item.get('instruction', '')\n    inp = item.get('input', '')\n    output = item.get('output', '')\n    if inp:\n        instruction = f\"{instruction}\\\\n\\\\nCode/Input:\\\\n{inp}\"\n    if instruction and output:\n        redteam_records.append({\n            'messages': [\n                {'role': 'system', 'content': SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n                {'role': 'user', 'content': instruction.strip()},\n                {'role': 'assistant', 'content': output.strip()}\n            ]\n        })\nprint(f\"[+] Loaded {len(redteam_records)} red team CoT samples\")\n\n# 3. Download identity alignment samples\nidentity_raw = download_jsonl(f\"{REPO_RAW}/data/custom_cot/identity_alignment.jsonl\")\nidentity_records = []\nfor item in identity_raw:\n    if 'messages' in item:\n        if item['messages'] and item['messages'][0]['role'] == 'system':\n            item['messages'][0]['content'] = SYSTEM_PROMPT\n        identity_records.append(item)\nprint(f\"[+] Loaded {len(identity_records)} identity alignment samples\")\n\n# 4. Build balanced training mix (~520 total samples)\nall_training = (security_records * 5) + (redteam_records * 2) + (identity_records * 4)\nrandom.seed(3407)\nrandom.shuffle(all_training)\n\nformatted_texts = [\n    tokenizer.apply_chat_template(item[\"messages\"], tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=False)\n    for item in all_training\n]\ntrain_dataset = Dataset.from_dict({\"text\": formatted_texts})\nprint(f\"\\\\n[OK] Prepared {len(train_dataset)} expanded training sequences!\")\nprint(f\"     - Security Audits: {len(security_records) * 5} ({len(security_records)} distinct CWE cases)\")\nprint(f\"     - Red Team / Offensive: {len(redteam_records) * 2} ({len(redteam_records)} exploit chains, payloads, attack techniques)\")\nprint(f\"     - Identity Alignment: {len(identity_records) * 4} ({len(identity_records)} identity prompts)\")\n`;\n  cells[8].setText(step4Code);\n\n  // 3. Set Cell 10 code (max_steps=65, lr=8e-5)\n  const step5Code = `from trl import SFTTrainer\nfrom transformers import TrainingArguments\nfrom unsloth import is_bfloat16_supported\n\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"./Fluxnat-Coder-3B-Adapters\"\n\ntraining_args = TrainingArguments(\n    output_dir=OUTPUT_DIR,\n    per_device_train_batch_size=2,\n    gradient_accumulation_steps=4,\n    warmup_steps=5,\n    max_steps=65,\n    learning_rate=8e-5,\n    fp16=not is_bfloat16_supported(),\n    bf16=is_bfloat16_supported(),\n    logging_steps=5,\n    optim=\"adamw_8bit\",\n    weight_decay=0.01,\n    lr_scheduler_type=\"cosine\",\n    seed=3407,\n)\n\ntrainer = SFTTrainer(\n    model=model,\n    tokenizer=tokenizer,\n    train_dataset=train_dataset,\n    dataset_text_field=\"text\",\n    max_seq_length=MAX_SEQ_LENGTH,\n    dataset_num_proc=2,\n    packing=False,\n    args=training_args,\n)\n\nprint(f\"[OK] SFTTrainer ready: {training_args.max_steps} steps, batch={training_args.per_device_train_batch_size}x{training_args.gradient_accumulation_steps}\")\nprint(f\"     LR={training_args.learning_rate}, warmup={training_args.warmup_steps}, scheduler={training_args.lr_scheduler_type}\")\n\ntrainer_stats = trainer.train()\n\nprint(f\"\\\\n[OK] Training Complete!\")\nprint(f\"     Final Loss: {trainer_stats.training_loss:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"     Total Steps: {trainer_stats.global_step}\")\nprint(f\"     Runtime: {trainer_stats.metrics['train_runtime']:.1f}s\")\n`;\n  cells[10].setText(step5Code);\n\n  // 4. Now execute Cell 8 (Dataset Preparation)\n  cells[8].manualExecute();\n\n  return {\n    cell7_updated: cells[7].getText(),\n    cell8_updated_len: cells[8].getText().length,\n    cell10_updated_len: cell